    "body": "It seems to work fine, but the `random` approach is barely faster for me. My solution without `string sub` appears to be a bit faster:\r\n| Command | Mean [ms] | Min [ms] | Max [ms] | Relative |\r\n|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| `fish -c 'export X=(starship session)'` | 6.2 ± 1.1 | 4.8 | 10.7 | 1.06 ± 0.26 |\r\n| `fish -c 'export X=(string sub -s1 -l16 (random)(random)(random)(random)(random)0000000000000000)'` | 6.0 ± 0.8 | 4.9 | 9.1 | 1.03 ± 0.22 |\r\n| `fish -c 'export X=(random 1000 9999)(random 1000 9999)(random 1000 9999)(random 1000 9999)'` | 5.8 ± 1.0 | 4.6 | 9.7 | 1.00 |\r\n\r\nEdit:\r\n\r\nI just tested it again on a different system and the change is more pronounced but still very small (also the string sub version is faster for some reason):\r\n| Command | Mean [ms] | Min [ms] | Max [ms] | Relative |\r\n|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| `fish -c 'export X=(starship session)'` | 8.9 ± 0.3 | 8.2 | 10.0 | 1.23 ± 0.07 |\r\n| `fish -c 'export X=(string sub -s1 -l16 (random)(random)(random)(random)(random)0000000000000000)'` | 7.2 ± 0.3 | 6.6 | 8.9 | 1.00 |\r\n| `fish -c 'export X=(random 1000 9999)(random 1000 9999)(random 1000 9999)(random 1000 9999)'` | 8.1 ± 1.1 | 6.4 | 11.5 | 1.13 ± 0.16 |\r\n\r\n\r\nEdit:\r\none more system::\r\n\r\n| Command | Mean [ms] | Min [ms] | Max [ms] | Relative |\r\n|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| `fish -c 'export X=(starship session)'` | 7.1 ± 1.0 | 6.3 | 18.8 | 1.52 ± 0.50 |\r\n| `fish -c 'export X=(string sub -s1 -l16 (random)(random)(random)(random)(random)0000000000000000)'` | 5.1 ± 0.6 | 4.5 | 13.4 | 1.09 ± 0.36 |\r\n| `fish -c 'export X=(random 1000 9999)(random 1000 9999)(random 1000 9999)(random 1000 9999)'` | 4.6 ± 1.4 | 4.1 | 31.0 | 1.00 |\r\n",
